A||||7||FieroSoul||Another A/C question||||6||
Z||000000||FieroSoul||08-15-2001||01:00 PM|||| I can feel a drag almost like a miss with my A/C on in my 2.5.  I can also hear a whirring sound most of the time.  Is this common with the dukes or is it a symptom of a problem like an A/C low on charge, locking up, etc.  It also seems to cycle quite often but still blows cold as ice.  Any ideas?||||reg||6
Z||000001||Voytek||08-15-2001||01:21 PM||||You know what?  I just fixed my A/C system in my '87 GT and it does the same thing.  This is a brand new compressor.  It blows nice and cold, everything seems to work properly but I DO hear the whirring sound, especially with higher RPM.  It's annoying and sounds like something's wrong.  The drag is definitely there when the compressor kicks in but that's normal.<BR>Can anyone else comment on how their A/C works?<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/voyteks_sig2.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||FieroSoul||08-15-2001||06:31 PM||||!!Bumpo!!||||reg||1
Z||000003||theogre||08-15-2001||07:48 PM||||That would be the AC clutch cycling. It's normal for that type setup. The A6 family compressors take significant power to kick over.<P>Only 87-88 4 cyl use the one that doesn't cycle the clutch. (If an OE 87-88 4 cyl AC clutch cycles, something is wrong with the system.)<P>As for wirring noise,,, if you have the AC on max cool then it's quite loud as the blower is right next to the inside intake.<p>[This message has been edited by theogre (edited 08-15-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||kiteman||08-15-2001||08:45 PM||||How often can it cycle and still be normal? Mine cycles about every 10 secs at highway speeds.  Cooling is a little weak on really hot days. I have an '84.||||reg||5
Z||000005||FieroSoul||08-16-2001||01:19 PM||||  Ditto to Kitmans question.  Seems like excessive cycling in my 84 too.||||reg||6
Z||000006||Patrick86GT||08-16-2001||04:11 PM||||I have only 86 & newer GT's for reference. Under the normal setting, the clutch cycle is about every 10 seconds and does put a slight "drag" on the 2.8's.  <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000007||theogre||08-16-2001||08:35 PM||||Cycle rate depends on a whole bunch of things. temperature, humidity, amount of refrigerant, AC control setting.....||||reg||1
